API Layer
The API layer serves as the primary entry point for external interactions with the platform, providing a secure and controlled interface for all incoming requests. This layer consists of two critical components:
Component
Version
Description
Access Rules
API Gateway
v1.2.3
Handles incoming traffic routing and rate limiting
Requires valid JWT token, rate limited to 500 req/min per client
Authentication Service
v2.1.0
Manages authentication and authorization
HTTPS required, supports OAuth2 and OpenID Connect

The API Gateway implements sophisticated rate limiting algorithms to prevent abuse while ensuring fair usage distribution across clients. It maintains a sliding window counter that tracks requests per client ID, automatically blocking traffic when limits are exceeded. The Authentication Service implements industry-standard protocols with support for custom authentication schemes, enabling seamless integration with existing identity providers while maintaining strict security standards.
