The Microservices Cluster operates within a Kubernetes environment, utilizing advanced orchestration techniques to maintain optimal resource utilization and service availability. The cluster implements rolling updates, self-healing capabilities, and automatic scaling based on workload demands. The Redis Cache layer employs advanced clustering configurations for high availability, implementing sophisticated key distribution algorithms to ensure optimal performance across distributed nodes.
