The Kubernetes infrastructure maintains strict RBAC controls, implementing least-privilege access principles across all administrative operations. The Object Storage system employs server-side encryption with customer-managed keys, supporting both fine-grained bucket policies and lifecycle management rules for optimal storage utilization and compliance requirements.
