SDK Architecture
The SDK implements a modular architecture that mirrors the platform's structure while providing a simplified interface for developers. The architecture consists of four main layers:
Client Layer
Handles API communication and authentication
Manages request/response lifecycle
Implements retry logic and error handling
Service Layer
Contains business logic implementations
Provides resource-specific operations
Handles data transformation
Data Layer
Manages data models and schemas
Handles data validation
Implements data serialization
Infrastructure Layer
Provides utility functions
Manages configuration
Handles logging and monitoring
Installation
The SDK is available through multiple package managers:

# Python
pip install ghi-platform-sdk

# Node.js
npm install @ghi-platform/sdk

# Java (Maven)
<dependency>
    <groupId>com.ghi.platform</groupId>
    <artifactId>sdk</artifactId>
    <version>1.0.0</version>
</dependency>
Getting Started
Initialize the SDK with your credentials:

from ghi_platform import Client

# Initialize client
client = Client(
    api_key="your_api_key",
    environment="production",
    region="us-west-1"
)

Core Features
Authentication
The SDK supports multiple authentication methods:

# API Key Authentication
client = Client(api_key="your_api_key")

# OAuth2 Authentication
client = Client(
    client_id="your_client_id",
    client_secret="your_client_secret",
    token_url="https://auth.example.com/token"
)

Data Management
The SDK provides comprehensive data management capabilities:

# Create a new resource
resource = client.resources.create(
    name="example-resource",
    data={
        "field1": "value1",
        "field2": "value2"
    }
)

# Retrieve a resource
resource = client.resources.get(resource_id="123")

# Update a resource
resource = client.resources.update(
    resource_id="123",
    data={
        "field1": "new-value"
    }
)

# Delete a resource
client.resources.delete(resource_id="123")


DATA / File Operations

# Upload a file
file = client.storage.upload(
    file_path="path/to/file.txt",
    content_type="text/plain"
)

# Download a file
client.storage.download(
    file_id="file-123",
    destination_path="downloaded_file.txt"
)

Error Handling
The SDK implements comprehensive error handling with specific exception types:

try:
    resource = client.resources.get(resource_id="123")
except ghi_platform.exceptions.ResourceNotFoundError:
    print("Resource not found")
except ghi_platform.exceptions.AuthenticationError:
    print("Authentication failed")
except ghi_platform.exceptions.RateLimitExceeded:
    print("Rate limit exceeded")

